{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/supportedversions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SupportedVersions","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The floor enforces itself: SwiftPM reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift-tools-version"},{"type":"text","text":" before it resolves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"anything, and an older toolchain refuses the package outright with a clear message."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Nothing enforces the upper end — a package resolves and builds on a newer toolchain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not anybody ever compiled it there, and the differences that matter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(strict concurrency, "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inference, isolation checking) are exactly the ones"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that surface as errors only once someone tries."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These values name both ends, so a build script or a compatibility note can report the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range without hardcoding numbers that go stale."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"One manifest, Swift 6 language mode","anchor":"One-manifest-Swift-6-language-mode","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The package ships a single "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at tools-version 6.2, and every target in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it is compiled in "},{"type":"strong","i